A1. An overhead twist. ~ BRAID
A5. What brings in the shekels? ~ LABOR
A9. An owlish question. ~ WHO
A12. Sea legs. ~ OARS
A13. This goes up in smoke at a conference. ~ CIGAR
A14. The ground covered by a camel. ~ ARID
A15. A bum accelerator to have in your car. ~ GIN
A16. An influence bachelors should beware of. ~ LUNAR
A17. The kind of men who own corporations. ~ OBESE
A18. This takes a sharp fall every winter. ~ SNOW
A20. What to fly into when you run out of gas. ~ PET
A21. Shadow casters before. ~ EVENTS
A22. This means maybe. ~ IF
A24. Something Dumb Dora lacks. ~ SENSE
A25. Mushy spot. ~ SETTEE
A29. Men of leisure. ~ TRAMPS
A34. The inner lining of a Southern coat. ~ TAR
A35. How Hoover stands with Republicans. ~ ERECT
A39. A distinguished feature that is not a nose. ~ TRAIT
A40. A solo flight. ~ ARIA
A42. The name of a Frog. ~ RAOUL
A44. Don't try to do this in a minute. ~ MILE
A45. The sort of woman who changes color easily. ~ BLOND
A47. A medieval Hood. ~ ROBIN
A49. The kind of girl most popular with a bachelor. ~ NEW
A50. Where doctors confine their mistakes. ~ SYSTEM
A52. Compulsion (And we don't mean Scott's Compulsion, Dora!) ~ DURESS
A54. The kind of check most easily cashed. ~ VALID
A57. This was discovered 439 years ago. ~ NA
A58. This is a hair raiser. ~ SPIRIT
A62. A hard rider. ~ RIM
A64. This always comes in on time. ~ TIDE
A68. Cheerful notes. ~ CAROL
A69. All wet. ~ BANAL
A70. A by way. ~ VIA
A71. This is burning matter. ~ ACID
A72. The kind of officer a girl adores. ~ PETTY
A73. Ritzy market. ~ MART
A74. Things women are always clamoring for (abbr.). ~ RTS
A75. Hymenoptera juice. ~ HONEY
A76. This is where the kick came. ~ PANTS

D1. Wet spots the Drys can't get at. ~ BOGS
D2. A street cleaner. ~ RAIN
D3. Vanderbilt's sparring partner. ~ ARNO
D4. A backward hick. ~ IS
D5. These were laid out on the gridiron. ~ LINES
D6. A little boy's jewel. ~ AGATE
D7. Where they used to hold old-fashioned setting-up exercises. ~ BAR
D8. A little connection. ~ OR
D9. A natty bird. ~ WREN
D10. A stop signal. ~ HIST
D11. Poetical shorts. ~ ODES
D13. This can certainly hold its liquor. ~ CUP
D14. An Irish Rose selection. ~ ABE
